   "design": "Middleware autoverification rules for ranges, delta checks, flags and QC status release results that pass every rule, under a rule version the clinical chemist approves before it goes live. The technologist reviews only the held results, so far fewer results need a look, though each takes longer. QC review, lookups, repeats, ward calls, the chemist talk, the check and release of held results stay with the technologist.",
   "previous_blocker": "About half of all results were held for review by hand.",
   "enabler_now": "Rule-based autoverification in lab middleware.",
   "still_hard": "Results that pass rules but do not fit the patient.",
   "human_edge": "Knowing when a normal-looking result is wrong.",
